WEBVTT

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:09.270
<i>Some time had passed since Ringo transferred to Tamo Agricultural.</i>

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.540
Wait for me, Young Master!

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.560
There's no need to rush.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.840
<i>Much like the people who enter our lives,</i>

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:38.800
<i>discoveries always come unexpected.</i>

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.280
<i>With each new one, all we can do
is stand in wonderment.</i>

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:17.190
The hell is this?!

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.280
Sheesh, what a mess.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.000
Has someone called the police?

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.160
I expected this would happen eventually.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.520
That's what you get for
not fencing off the field.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.680
Are there any witnesses?

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:29.710
Any testimony is valuable.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:32.160
<i>I</i> saw it.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:36.220
Indeed, I can say with
certainty it was a child.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.180
A child?

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:41.860
It ran by, arms full of vegetables,
wearing what looked like a gray coat.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.540
A-And what time was this?

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:48.240
It happened yesterday, on my way back from tending to the cows,

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.940
so sometime past eight PM.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.650
It dropped this as it left.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.640
It seems we have a lead.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.610
So what do you plan to do
about this, Kamatori Kei?

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.910
If it's a child, we'll need to investigate their motives and actions with utmost care.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.660
While it might have been mischief,

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:07.420
for all we know they were starving to death.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.840
Patrasche, I'm so tired.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:14.220
Setsuko! Hanako! The Little Match Girl!
The Happy Prince's swallow!

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:17.500
It's always the frail and innocent who meet with tragic ends!

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.460
Hey, y'all.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:20.520
What, Nakazawa Minori?

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.920
Kamatori Kei and I are discussing a potential social issue of—

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.430
Warn't this done by a monkey?

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:27.640
A monkey?

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.260
Kousaku, don't it look like a monkey?

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.020
Yeah, seems like it.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.680
But wait. It was walking on two feet.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.480
Wild monkeys can do that,
if'n it's only for a bit.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.820
Yeah, as they make off with
a watermelon or something.

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:43.070
Y-You've seen it happen?!

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:47.300
Well, me and Minori are from about the most rural village you can imagine.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.760
We had dogs, monkeys, and pheasants too.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.250
Next you'll say you had a giant peach!

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.760
Ah, thank goodness.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.820
We don't have to call UNICEF.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:57.250
Well, nothing to see here, then.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.010
What is it?

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:04.220
Oh, just steeling ourselves
for the coming battle.

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:07.810
Bring it!

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:12.230
All right.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:17.580
Let's begin the first Forum on How to
Deal with That Monkey 'Cause It's a Pain.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:22.860
Let's hear your
suggestions one at a time.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:23.640
Okay!

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:24.950
So my plan is...

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:36.880
Back home, we used to surround the fields with 'lectric fences.

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:37.780
Electric...

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:38.840
You shocked them?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.670
Not enough to kill them.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.390
Let's put this plan in action at once!

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.380
While it's certainly a fine solution,

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:48.140
it's not possible.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:49.740
Why not?

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:53.350
Our budget.

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:54.500
'Kay, next!

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:03.030
I think we should leave
some food out for it.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.410
It must be hungry.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.040
I get it!

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:15.040
If its belly's full up on grub,
it'll leave the fields be.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.160
Indeed!

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.170
Let's put this plan in action at once!

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.510
It's not a bad idea,

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:25.590
but it's not just the orchards
and fields that are being hit.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.640
The damage is clearly part mischief.

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.640
I doubt satiating its hunger
will stop the vandalism.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.600
Sheesh, Mr. Smarty-Pants Kei!

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:42.260
I, Hata Kousaku, age 16,

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:46.700
have devoted the greater half of my life
to the war against monkeys.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:47.540
Behold!

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.920
This baby is Super Hitoshi-kun!

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:51.820
Thirty times the firepower
of the previous generation!

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:55.070
It fires thirty firework
rockets in one round!

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:57.080
It looks formidable indeed.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:00.470
We'll send those monkeys
home with PTSD!

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:12.680
Huh?

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:14.420
That's funny.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.540
I reckon the gunpowder's wet.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.260
Lemme take a look-see.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:32.640
K-Kids, don't never look down the barrel of a weapon.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:34.160
Don't do it! Ever!

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:35.660
Bam!

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.140
Foolish plebeians.

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:41.540
It seems you require my genius!

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:43.790
So what is this genius plan?

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:51.760
Listen well, peasants.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.100
Monkeys and humans are both primates.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.060
If we open our arms and
hearts and talk it over—

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:57.300
Rejected!

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.730
N-Now shee here...

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:04.540
we humansh are primatesh too...

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.520
Hunter?

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:04.540
Yes.

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.730
If we talk it over... I'm shure...

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.740
Fortunately, we only have
one monkey to deal with.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.140
If we exterminate it,
our problems are solved.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.280
Exterminate...

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:16.880
K-Kei, killing the monkey's gonna leave a really bad aftertaste.

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:18.900
Agriculture can be cruel.

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:22.640
I, for one, am prepared
to do what must be done.

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:25.540
All right...

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.670
I happen to be acquainted
with a skilled hunter.

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:29.700
Leave this matter in my hands.

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:37.100
Heya. Name's Oomori.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.160
Who's this creepy old—

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:42.700
Whoa!

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:44.180
Have a little tact, Ringo.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:45.920
Who's <i>this</i> creepy old guy
supposed to be?

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:47.940
Watch your mouth, Tits!

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.400
What is the meaning of this, Kamatori Kei?

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.360
Just when I had my hopes up after you said you knew someone,

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:55.200
you bring <i>this</i> nerd?

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.080
We judge people based
90% on appearances,

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.910
which leaves 10% to surprise us.

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:04.790
This may surprise you,
but Oomori-san is a blowgun expert.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:06.380
A blowgun expert?

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:12.880
I'm the sugoi founder of
the Oomori Blowgun Style.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:14.620
"Sugoi"?

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:18.350
By the way, where's your blowgun?

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:20.110
Right here uguu!

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:26.260
Those are blowguns?

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:28.480
They're sniper blowguns desu.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.070
Sniper blowguns?

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.080
A-Are they?

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:37.020
Man, here I thought they were
anime posters or something!

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:40.240
No, these <i>are</i> kawaii anime posters.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:44.380
I use rolled-up anime posters as blowgun pipes.

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:46.760
O-Oh, I see!

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:52.640
So may I ask what you usually hunt with your blowguns?

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:55.590
The occasional normalfag.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:59.000
R-Really? Gosh...

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:57.340
"Normalfag"?

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:59.020
"Normalfag", he says.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:04.580
S-So, if you don't mind me asking, what do you do for a living?

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:01.080
Don'tcha reckon this guy's trouble?

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.480
What's a "normalfag"?

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.850
No job, bro.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:19.140
The sugoi tranquilizer
I've brewed is enough

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:22.040
to put any monkey-tan
out of commission!

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:25.740
Ah-ah, the name of
the product is a secret desu!

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:30.920
Here it comes!

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:39.040
This stance makes you look like you're eating a giant lollipop,

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.620
so I call it the Lolli-Licking Stance!

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:42.600
Good for you.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:53.860
That was the Normalfag Kill—

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.320
I don't wanna hear it!

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:55.320
Let's go.

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:59.300
You're in for the walloping
of your life, monkey!

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:00.490
Get 'im good!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.920
Look, his arm...

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:18.080
Kousaku?

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:21.510
You can't let yourself
feel sorry for it, Ringo.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:23.590
Darn tootin'.

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:25.720
We gotta worry first
'bout protectin' the crops.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:37.540
I don't know if his injury
was the reason for

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:39.800
or the result of being
abandoned by his troop,

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.160
but one way or another, he's an outcast.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:46.140
We may as well start thinking about how to do away with him.

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:48.620
Yoshida, that's not something to act so gleeful about.

00:10:48.620 --> 00:10:50.980
Foolish as ever, Kamatori Kei.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:54.170
I already have a proposal for this monkey's ultimate fate.

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:59.820
I've asked an acquaintance who
works at a zoo if they'll take him.

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:02.320
I see. A zoo.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:03.360
That's right.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:06.480
Currently, they have only
females in their enclosure.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:11.270
This male would be readily accepted and surely become a fruitful sire.

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:13.120
That's a relief!

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:16.480
He'll be a new man—
I mean monkey in there!

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.040
My apologies, Yoshida.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:18.940
We are in your debt.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:22.260
Wh-Whadyoo mean d-dwebt?

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:26.200
I-It's nyot wike I did it to
impwesh you or anyfwing!

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.700
I-It wash to hewp the monkey!

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:41.260
I thought so.

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:46.680
Comin'!

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:49.680
You hollered, Kousaku?

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:52.100
Mind if I come in?

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:53.440
I've got something important to discuss.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.500
Can you come back in one hour?

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:00.960
I'd prefer right now...

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:01.880
Numskull!

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.280
This ain't somethin' you do
with no prep'ration!

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:04.990
Gimme a bit.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:08.260
"One hour"?

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:13.200
I'm ready!

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:14.720
'Kay, I'm coming in!

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:23.010
W-Welcome, Kou-tan.

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:25.020
Did you redecorate?

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:28.180
Y-Yeah, but don't mind it, and relax.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.760
You need to shower?

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:30.970
Nah, I'm good.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:34.780
Meanin' you wanna do it
together when we're done?!

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:36.920
Oh, Kei's here.

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:37.540
Kei?

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:39.300
Yeah, I invited him.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:39.820
Come in!

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.190
Don't mind if I—

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:44.070
She redecorated.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.800
It was supposed to be yes...

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.520
to be yes...

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:49.120
I see.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:52.130
Kou-tan, what didja need to discuss?

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:55.060
Right, it's about Ringo.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:58.960
G'night.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:12:59.720
Go die!

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:02.420
What, why? I haven't said anything yet!

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:03.860
Die, and I ain't bein' tsundere!

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:06.150
I plan on living!
What's wrong with you, anyway?

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:08.440
You're really asking for a "nice boat" end.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:09.440
Why a nice bo—

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:11.560
Whatever, just take a look at this.

00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:14.240
Here I go, everyone!

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:16.020
Sing along with me!

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:19.590
This is... one of Kusakabe Yuka's DVDs?

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:21.400
I thought I done got everything.

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.440
You still managed to hide one?

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.720
I bought a new copy with my allowance!

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:27.720
Anyway, look at Yuka-tan.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:28.870
Do you notice anything?

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:36.080
Well, to state the obvious,
she looks quite cheerful and pleasant.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:39.320
It's hard to believe she and
Kinoshita are the same person.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:40.230
Darn tootin'.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:41.760
She's got a million-dollar smile.

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:42.880
Exactly!

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:45.000
She's smiling!

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:48.590
I haven't seen her smile once
since she came here!

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:50.850
Not when she introduced herself,

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:51.850
nor during the panties incident,

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:52.810
nor while we were eating,

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:54.390
nor during the King Game,

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:56.140
nor when she held her own against Minori,

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:57.670
nor when the monkey was saved.

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:59.810
Ringo never so much as smirked!

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:03.190
Sure, but ain't this here her stage smile?

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:09.450
Well yeah, but isn't it depressing to live with someone who never smiles?

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:11.830
I s'pose so.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:12.660
Right?

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:14.080
Understood.

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:17.790
If it's laughs you want,
look no further than yours truly!

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:24.710
Fancy running into you here, Kinoshita.

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:28.010
By the way, would you like to see a short comedy routine?

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.340
Okay.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:35.810
Dark matter!

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:39.310
And?

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.070
Looks like we gotta get our hands dirty.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.050
Kinoshita-san!

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:54.930
Cootchie-cootchie-coo!

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:55.850
Damn you, Minori!

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:57.750
How I wish I were in your shoes!

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.080
But good going!

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:02.130
How'dya like my technique, missy?

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.290
Come on, come on!

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:07.070
Awright, how 'bout here?

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:08.010
Or here?

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:09.510
You like it here?

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.220
N-Not there...

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.700
Your body doesn't lie.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:17.610
Go on, give into it.

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:19.730
Lose yourself to
pleasure's sweet embrace!

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:21.940
I'm losing myself!

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:25.190
You done had enough? Give up?

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:30.030
Now it's my turn.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:34.970
Sto... Sto...!

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:38.740
Can'... breah...

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:49.920
What are you playing at?

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:55.140
I-I was just, well...

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:57.850
You're always so expressionless,

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.600
so I was worried you weren't enjoying yourself here.

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:03.810
So...

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:07.330
you tried to make me laugh?

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:08.270
I'm sorry.

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:10.570
I didn't mean any harm. I just...

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:13.550
I guess we got carried away.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.530
I <i>can't</i> laugh.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:19.450
Neither laugh nor smile.

00:16:25.600 --> 00:16:29.550
At first, they just said
I looked a bit gloomy.

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:34.260
Everyone simply chalked it up to exhaustion.

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:41.670
But soon enough, I couldn't smile no matter how hard I tried.

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:44.690
My other expressions
followed soon after,

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:48.150
and I found myself with no place where I'd once belonged—

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:51.020
just like that monkey.

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:54.790
B-But the monkey found a home!

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:56.110
I'm sure you can...

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.170
Thank you.

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.540
I'm sorry.

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:15.750
Is it really possible to forget how to smile?

00:17:15.750 --> 00:17:19.640
I can't say for sure, but there must be some psychological factor at play.

00:17:21.440 --> 00:17:23.100
Kusakabe Yuka...

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:28.810
Kinoshita Ringo may have been worn out by the expectations of others.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:32.210
Then she'll be right as rain
if she rests a spell?

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:34.510
Who can say?

00:17:34.510 --> 00:17:36.100
I want to see her smile.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:41.280
We all do, but are we just being selfish?

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:54.570
<i>Kousaku...</i>

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:55.840
<i>Kousaku!</i>

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:00.610
Young Master?

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:02.720
<i>I am not Young Master.</i>

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:05.510
<i>I am... Gaia.</i>

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:06.480
Gaia?!

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:11.090
<i>Yes. I am here to deliver a message to you.</i>

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:12.660
A-A message?

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:16.390
<i>Look inside yourself, Kousaku.</i>

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:20.150
<i>Remember what you humans have done to me.</i>

00:18:20.150 --> 00:18:24.370
<i>And remember where you are now.</i>

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:27.840
<i>Don't forget, Kousaku.</i>

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:32.650
<i>Gaia is always near,
quietly urging you to plant and cultivate.</i>

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:36.050
W-Wait, Young—Gaia!

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:39.090
Gaia!

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.230
What in the world was that?

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:57.900
She asked me to remember what mankind did to Gaia.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:16.420
I'm thinking we should bring Ringo there,

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.880
so she can see the soil.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:24.150
I can see why that place
might resonate with her.

00:19:24.150 --> 00:19:25.250
Darn tootin'.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:29.810
She'll prob'ly gain somethin'
valuable from seein' it.

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:38.750
Agricultural high schools often have an Agricultural Club, or AC.

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:43.160
We're on our way to visit a project that past students began for us.

00:19:43.540 --> 00:19:44.670
A project?

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:48.010
Yep. We thought you might want to join.

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:56.650
Here?

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:57.470
Yep.

00:19:57.470 --> 00:19:59.490
Not the tomato patch?

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:00.810
No, here first.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:05.770
Feel the soil.

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:06.670
The soil?

00:20:06.670 --> 00:20:07.410
Yeah.

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.870
It's hard and crumbly.

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:20.890
Right, the soil here is dead.

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:22.070
Dead?

00:20:22.600 --> 00:20:24.910
Nothing will grow here.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.120
That's why we say it's dead.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:28.750
Why?

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:30.370
They didn't rotate their crops.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.090
Remember learning about that?

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:38.290
If you keep planting the same crop in the same area, it eventually stops growing.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:39.750
Precisely.

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:44.530
But the short-sighted fools tried to offset the declining harvest

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:46.850
by feeding the land chemical fertilizer.

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:49.530
Their reward: an infestation of pests.

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:51.430
Then, an overdose of pesticide.

00:20:52.400 --> 00:20:55.140
Before us is the result of
this comedy of errors.

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:03.110
Will this soil never get better again?

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:12.670
This field over here
started out just like that one.

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:15.040
Actually, they were once a single field.

00:21:15.820 --> 00:21:19.230
Our predecessors in
the AC took on this project,

00:21:19.230 --> 00:21:21.130
and we're continuing it.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:24.050
It took us seven years to reach this point.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.550
Seven years...

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:30.260
Of course, it's not fully restored.

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:34.290
Even so, these plants are digging deep

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:36.800
to bring life from this weary land.

00:21:41.630 --> 00:21:44.820
Then... this land will be reborn?

00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:22.450
Hey, can I try one of those tomatoes?

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:24.100
Now?

00:22:24.100 --> 00:22:25.110
I want to taste one.

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:26.430
All right.

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:32.430
Here.

00:22:42.620 --> 00:22:43.870
It's bitter...

00:22:43.870 --> 00:22:45.550
That one's not ripe yet.

00:22:46.260 --> 00:22:47.800
But I'll eat it.

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:53.690
It's really bitter.

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:54.720
I bet.

00:22:55.060 --> 00:22:55.990
But...

00:22:57.940 --> 00:22:59.330
it tastes wonderful.

00:23:02.440 --> 00:23:04.560
Ringo, you just—

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:07.930
K-Kinoshita-san! Here!

00:23:07.930 --> 00:23:09.430
Have this'un too!

00:23:09.430 --> 00:23:10.860
This one's redder!

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:12.930
Kinoshita-san, how 'bout this'un?

00:23:12.930 --> 00:23:15.330
It's ripened up mighty nice!

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:16.330
Or how does this one look?

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:18.630
<i>Crops raised with love and care</i>

00:23:18.630 --> 00:23:23.520
<i>provide happiness and nourishment for both body and soul.</i>

00:23:23.520 --> 00:23:27.210
<i>But more than anything,
there is joy in raising them.</i>

00:23:27.640 --> 00:23:31.800
<i>I can only hope that someday,
you'll know that joy too.</i>

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:39.650
"The Four Farm Deity Quintet".
